-- title:
--   Affine Drinfeld chart at a supersingular place, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix the prime $q$ with $q=2$, an integer $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Further data: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of the base-changed modular function field, compatible via `hR₀` with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$; an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity; families $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O^{\mathrm{ss}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the description of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of non-zero reduction, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action through `levelAutBar` together with injectivity and permutation of the $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, the contraction $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)\cap\overline{\mathbb Q}=A$, the compatibility `hSS_over` of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ with the reduction $R_0$ at the place $s$ (including that differences with Teichmüller-type representatives lie in the maximal ideal), $\Gamma_0(M')$-invariance of each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, and existence for each $s$ of $t\in O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ with $t-a$ a unit for all $a\in A$. Finally: a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image is $A\cap K_0$, with surjective induced residue map, uniformiser $\varpi_0$ satisfying $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$; the subfield $F_0\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of the modular invariant $j$; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ given by $\iota$; and a place $s\in W$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an $A_0$-subalgebra $B\subseteq F_0$ which is finitely generated, integrally closed in $F_0$ (every $x\in F_0$ integral over $B$ lies in $B$), has $F_0$ as its field of fractions, such that every non-maximal prime of $B$ containing $\varpi_0 B$ is a minimal prime of $\varpi_0 B$, every non-zero prime $\mathfrak p$ not containing $\varpi_0 B$ has localisation $B_{\mathfrak p}$ equal to a valuation subring of $F_0$, and: $\hat\jmath\in B$; $B\subseteq O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$; there is a prime $\mathfrak q_0$ with $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)\cap F_0=B_{\mathfrak q_0}$ and $\mathfrak q_0$ the only minimal prime of $\varpi_0 B$; $B\not\subseteq O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ for every $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$; $B\subseteq O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s')$ only for $s'=s$; $A_0\to B$ is formally smooth; and any finite set of valuation subrings $V$ of $F_0$, each contained in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)\cap F_0$ properly and not containing $B$, has at most $q+1$ elements.
--
--   This is the construction, in the case $q=2$ at the rigidifying auxiliary level provided by $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, of the affine Drinfeld chart of the descended semistable model of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular point: a normal finitely generated $A_0$-algebra whose localisation at the unique minimal prime over the uniformiser is the Drinfeld ring $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)\cap F_0$, lying in no Igusa ring and in no other Drinfeld ring, formally smooth over $A_0$, and meeting at most $q+1$ further valuation rings of $F_0$. It feeds the passage to the local ring of the Drinfeld chart on the normal model generated by $j$ in the same case.
-- source:
